Release audit at HEAD 5536313 (14 commits since 3e5e6b0). Every new ADR from tonight's work (0009-0028, except a few without a hyperlink) is referenced from woven POD as `L<docs/adr/NNNN|https://github.com/Getty/p5-file-sops/blob/main/docs/adr/NNNN-....md>`. origin/main currently only has docs/adr/0001-0008 (verified: `git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main -- docs/adr` = 8 files; local HEAD has 29). `git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD` = 58.

Empirically confirmed via `gh api repos/Getty/p5-file-sops/contents/...`: docs/adr/0008 -> 200 (exists on GitHub), docs/adr/0022 -> 404 Not Found. So right now every one of those ~17 GitHub links in the built POD is dead.

Neither xt/author-pod-syntax.t nor xt/author-pod-links.t (Pod::Checker, karr #98's fix) catches this: both check POD syntax / internal link resolution, neither performs an HTTP check on an external L<...|https://...> target. This is a real gap in the pre-release check, not just this one incident.

Action: push local main to origin (58 commits) before or as part of the next release, so the ADR links in the shipped POD resolve. Not a code/test blocker -- dzil build/dzil test/interop all pass clean at HEAD -- but a real documentation-quality gap a CPAN release would ship today.

